.\" Manpage for live-remaster
.\" Contact adrian@mxlinux.org for bug reports
.TH LIVE-REMASTER 1 "2026-01-09" "arch-remaster" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
live-remaster \- Regenerate airootfs.sfs on a running Arch Linux live system

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B live-remaster
.RB [options]

.SH DESCRIPTION
live-remaster recreates the compressed squashfs root filesystem on a running Arch Linux live system. It packages the current live environment as a new airootfs.sfs, optionally backing up and replacing the original. This tool is designed to be run from a live environment to remaster itself.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR -c , --comp <type>
Compression algorithm (default: zstd). Supported: gzip, lz4, xz, zstd
.TP
.BR -g
Use gzip compression (short option, stackable)
.TP
.BR -l
Use lz4 compression (short option, stackable)
.TP
.BR -x
Use xz compression (short option, stackable)
.TP
.BR -z
Use zstd compression (short option, stackable)
.TP
.BR -h , --help
Display help information
.TP
.BR -v , --version
Display version information
.TP
.BR -b , --no-backup
Skip backing up the original airootfs.sfs. Without this option, you will be prompted to backup if the file exists
.TP
.BR -m , --no-checksum , --no-md5sum
Skip checksum calculation. By default, the script writes
.I airootfs.sha512
using SHA-512. Can be stacked with other short options

.SH USAGE NOTES

.PP
The script should be run from a live Arch ISO booted system. It will:

.RS
.IP 1.
Detect if the live boot device is mounted at /run/archiso/bootmnt.
In copytoram mode, it attempts auto-detection via labels
ARCH_YYYYMM, ARCHISO_EFI, LIVE-UEFI, and MXarch-Live
.IP 2.
Calculate the size of the uncompressed root filesystem
.IP 3.
Create a new compressed squashfs image
.IP 4.
Optionally backup and replace the original airootfs.sfs
.RE

.SH EXCLUDED DIRECTORIES
The following directories are excluded from the squashfs:
.br
proc, sys, dev, tmp, mnt, media, lost+found, var/tmp, var/log, var/cache, var/lib/pacman/sync, run/*

.SH SPACE REQUIREMENTS
The script checks available space on the boot device before replacing the original file. A safety margin of 20 MiB is included. If insufficient space exists, the new file is left as airootfs.sfs.new for manual replacement.

.SH EXAMPLES

Remaster with default zstd compression:
.RS
.PP
.nf
sudo ./live-remaster
.fi
.RE

Remaster with xz compression and no backup:
.RS
.PP
.nf
sudo ./live-remaster -x -b
.fi
.RE

Stackable options (xz, no backup, no checksum):
.RS
.PP
.nf
sudo ./live-remaster -xbm
.fi
.RE

Display version:
.RS
.PP
.nf
./live-remaster -v
.fi
.RE

Display help:
.RS
.PP
.nf
./live-remaster -h
.fi
.RE

Use long options:
.RS
.PP
.nf
sudo ./live-remaster --comp gzip --no-backup --no-checksum
.fi
.RE

.SH REQUIREMENTS
The following programs must be available:
.br
mksquashfs, sha512sum

.SH SAFETY MARGIN
20 MiB is reserved as a safety margin when checking available space on the boot device.

